! A "$p" with no "$=" used to record a proof section of length -1.
! Each of these commands consumed that length in a different place and
! crashed: SHOW PROOF and SAVE PROOF through parseProof(), which sizes
! its work arrays from it, and both WRITE SOURCE forms through the
! memcpy() that copies the proof section into the output.
verify proof *
show statement z2 /full
show proof z2
save proof z2
write source proof-section-plain.mm
write source proof-section-out.mm /extract *
